  "term": "scanning",
  "definition": "Scanning here refers to a diagnostic imaging method that uses a small amount of radioactive tracer to show changes in an organ or body area. The tracer is swallowed or injected, then detected by a gamma camera and computer to create an image that can reveal problems such as cancer, injury, infection, or degeneration.",
